# React Router framework mode typegen output (Increment #40)
.react-router/

# The PRODUCTION BUILD OUTPUT, anchored to the frontend root with a
# leading slash (corrected in #45).
#
# A bare `build/` matches a directory named `build` at ANY depth, and
# this project has a second one: `src/build/`, which holds
# `prerenderPaths.ts` -- a load-bearing module that BOTH
# `react-router.config.ts` and `src/routes.ts` import at config time.
# It was therefore never committed, and a fresh clone of this repository
# could not build the frontend at all:
#
#   Error loading react-router.config.ts:
#   Cannot find module './src/build/prerenderPaths'
#
# Found in #45 while building HEAD in a clean worktree to measure a
# bundle delta. The leading slash anchors the pattern to this directory,
# so it still ignores the build output and no longer hides source.
/build/
